hat never parses untrusted\nimages and is absent from every deployed service runtime.\n\nRESOLUTIONS.md: dropped the brace-expansion entry (genuinely fixed at\n1.1.18, since the 1.x line received a backport in 1.1.16), corrected the\njsonpath-plus rationale (mosaic-cli now pulls @asyncapi/parser ^3.6.0; the\nvulnerable ^7.2.0 range now arrives via @asyncapi/multi-parser''s legacy\n2.1.2 and 3.0.0-next-major-spec.8 parsers), and re-verified the remaining\nupstream blockers (ajv, lodash, serialize-javascript, immutable~3.7.6) and\nthe deferred uuid/tmp entries as still blocked.\n\nNote: qs stays at 6.15.3 (2 moderate, npm-advisory-only). The upstream fix\nexists - express@4.22.3 moves to qs ~6.16.0 - but that release is newer\nthan this repo''s npmMinimalAgeGate: ''7d'' supply-chain gate, so Yarn\ncorrectly refused it. Documented with an explicit do-not-bypass note;\nre-run after 2026-09-21 to pick it up with no manifest change.\n\nVerification: yarn build (all services plus vod-to-live), tsc --noEmit\nover media-service including scripts/, yarn install --immutable, and 811\nunit tests across 54 files. DB integration tests could not run - the\nshared Postgres has leftover ddp_* databases from a sibling project that\nblock test:reset:dbs; this is pre-existing and unrelated to these changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: bump express/body-parser to clear both qs advisories\n\nThe 7-day npm age gate (npmMinimalAgeGate in .yarnrc.yml) has released\nexpress@4.22.3 and body-parser@1.20.8, both of which require qs@~6.16.0.\nDeleting the express, body-parser and qs@~6.15.1 lockfile entries and\nreinstalling picks up the fix with no manifest change.\n\nResolves the two moderate npm advisories left open by #607:\n- qs array-limit bypass via bracket-key comma parsing (>=6.14.2 <=6.15.3)\n- qs Denial of Service via attacker-controlled isBuffer (>=2.2.5 <6.16.0)\n\nAll qs copies are now 6.16.0. The age gate was not weakened or bypassed.\n\nVerified: yarn install --immutable passes, yarn build clean,\n54 test files / 811 tests passing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: raise engines.node to >=22 on all five services\n\nAddresses two Codex review findings on this PR: media-service and\nvod-to-live-service declared engines.node \">=18\" while depending on\npackages that require newer Node.\n\n- @faker-js/faker@10.6.0 (media-service, runtime dependency) requires\n  ^20.19.0 || ^22.13.0 || ^23.5.0 || >=24.0.0 AND is ESM-only\n  (\"type\": \"module\"). media-service compiles to CommonJS, so the built\n  output calls require(\"@faker-js/faker\"). That only works because\n  require(esm) is unflagged from Node 22.12; on Node 18 it is a hard\n  ERR_REQUIRE_ESM crash, not a warning.\n- xmlbuilder2@4.0.3 (vod-to-live, runtime dependency) requires >=20.0.\n- sharp@0.35.4 (media-service devDependency) requires >=20.9.0. Codex did\n  not flag this one, but it is the same class of problem.\n\nAll five services are bumped rather than only the two flagged, because\n\">=18\" was already inaccurate everywhere: catalog, channel and\nentitlement each depend on vitest, rimraf and jest-extended, which all\nrequire Node >=20. Previously only devDependencies violated the\ndeclaration, so a built service could still run on Node 18; the faker and\nxmlbuilder2 bumps made it a runtime violation for the first time.\n\n>=22 matches what the repository actually targets and tests: .nvmrc is\nv22, the Dockerfile builds on node:22-bookworm-slim, and every CI\nworkflow pins Node 22. No deployed runtime is affected - this corrects a\nstale manifest contract, it does not change behaviour.\n\nyarn.lock is unchanged. Verified: yarn install --immutable passes,\nyarn build clean (including vod-to-live), 54 test files / 811 tests\npassing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNAT